{"schema_version":"1.9.0","id":"OESA-2026-3632","published":"2026-09-05T15:03:20Z","modified":"2026-09-05T15:16:26.807040017Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-18917","CVE-2026-61477","CVE-2026-63622"],"summary":"libvirt security update","details":"Libvirt is a C toolkit to interact with the virtualization capabilities of recent versions of Linux (and other OSes). The main package includes the libvirtd server exporting the virtualization support.\r\n\r\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\nA flaw was found in libvirt. An unprivileged local user could exploit an integer overflow vulnerability in the NodeGetFreePages RPC handler. This flaw allows crafted values to bypass a size check, leading to an undersized memory buffer. Subsequently, real NUMA node data can overwrite this buffer. This heap buffer overflow can corrupt the root libvirt daemon&apos;s memory, potentially leading to a denial of service or local privilege escalation.(CVE-2026-18917)\n\nAn injection vulnerability was found in libvirt&apos;s virtual network driver. The network XML parser does not strip newline characters from DNS TXT record value attributes and SRV record domain/target attributes. These values are written verbatim into the dnsmasq configuration file generated by the network driver, allowing a user with permission to define virtual networks to inject arbitrary dnsmasq configuration directives such as dhcp-script, leading to arbitrary command execution as root.(CVE-2026-61477)\n\nA flaw was found in libvirt. A local attacker, specifically a process running as the confined `swtpm` user, could exploit a symlink-following vulnerability in the `virFileChownFiles()` function. By planting a symbolic link within the `swtpm` state directory, the attacker could trick the root-level libvirt daemon into changing the ownership of an arbitrary file to the `swtpm` user. This allows for privilege escalation from the `swtpm` sandbox to root-level file ownership control.(CVE-2026-63622)","affected":[{"package":{"name":"libvirt","ecosystem":"openEuler:20.03-LTS-SP4","purl":"pkg:rpm/openEuler/libvirt&distro=openEuler-20.03-LTS-SP4"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4"}]}],"ecosystem_specific":{"aarch64":["libvirt-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-admin-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-bash-completion-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-client-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-config-network-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-config-nwfilter-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-interface-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-network-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-nodedev-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-nwfilter-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-qemu-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-secret-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-storage-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-storage-core-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-storage-disk-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-storage-gluster-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-storage-iscsi-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-storage-iscsi-direct-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-storage-logical-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-storage-mpath-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-storage-rbd-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-driver-storage-scsi-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-kvm-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-daemon-qemu-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-debuginfo-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-debugsource-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-devel-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-docs-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarch64.rpm","libvirt-libs-6.2.0-28.oe2003sp4.aarc